# Python and tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.hypothesis/
.deepeval/
.coverage
coverage.xml
coverage.json
htmlcov/

# Everything under .cache/ is derived and rebuildable, so the directory is ignored
# rather than the two subdirectories inside it. Naming `vectors/` and `report/`
# individually meant a third cache -- and there will be a third cache -- arrived as
# untracked noise in everyone's `git status` until somebody thought to add a line.
.cache/

# Generated corpora. The tau2 corpus under data/tau2/ is vendored and tracked; this is
# for anything a CollectionSource of your own writes out.
data/corpus/

# Secrets. Never commit.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# tau2-bench vendored data (MIT, sierra-research/tau2-bench) - large task files
data/tau2/banking_knowledge/tasks_voice.json

# Build artefacts. A copy of src/atlas under another name is a second source of
# truth that nothing imports and that drifts silently; it was committed by accident.
build/
dist/

# Editor and agent state. Local to whoever is working, never to the repository.
# .claude/ was covered only by .git/info/exclude, which lives inside one clone and
# reaches nobody who clones this: every contributor would have seen it as untracked.
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# macOS. This repository is written on darwin, so these appear in every directory
# somebody opens in Finder, and a public repo collects them from contributors too.
.DS_Store
._*

# NOT ignored, deliberately, and listed here so nobody adds them by reflex:
#
#   data/results/runs.jsonl   every recorded run, one line each. Committed so a reader
#                             with no API key can print any table with
#                             `just report --render`, and so a change to a published
#                             number shows up in a diff.
#   data/labels.jsonl         human verdicts. Small, and the point of them is provenance.
#   data/noise_floor.json     the judge's disagreement with itself, from
#                             `just noise-floor`. Committed for the same reason
#                             runs.jsonl is: every judge relation in
#                             tests/measurement/test_judge.py is a multiple of it, and
#                             a threshold whose basis is not in the repository is a
#                             number somebody remembers.
#   data/coverage_baseline.json   one committed percentage, what scripts/coverage_delta.py
#                             compares a run against to catch a coverage regression. See
#                             docs/test-coverage.md for why this is a regression check and
#                             never an absolute floor.
#   uv.lock                   1403 hashed pins. Ignoring it would make the README's
#                             install path unreproducible.
